==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{stand sp|en|catalogue|from=US}}.

====Usage notes====
* In American English, both ''catalog'' and ''catalogue'' are in use; however, ''catalogue'' is largely confined to traditional or institutional contexts, while ''catalog'' is the more prevalent form in general usage.
* The spelling ''catalog'' has been attested since the 16th century, but it did not gain widespread popularity in the United States until the late 19th century.<ref name=etymonline>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref><ref name=gr>{{cite-web|en|title=Catalog vs. Catalogue|author=Angbeen Chaudhary|nodate=1|publisher=STANDS4 LLC|work=Grammar.com|titleurl=https://www.grammar.com/catalog_vs._catalogue|accessdate=20 April 2025|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240805093510/https://www.grammar.com/catalog_vs._catalogue|archivedate=5 August 2024}}</ref>
* Despite common assumptions, this spelling does not appear in any of Noah Webster’s dictionaries.<ref name=gr/>

